micro 2.0.15 — licences and sources

micro-2.0.15-linux64-static.tar.gz is the unmodified upstream static release:
https://github.com/micro-editor/micro/releases/download/v2.0.15/micro-2.0.15-linux64-static.tar.gz
solve.sh installs its micro executable without modification. SOURCE.json pins
the release checksum. The corresponding source for micro 2.0.15 is:
https://github.com/micro-editor/micro/archive/refs/tags/v2.0.15.tar.gz
Dependencies are identified by the release's go.mod and go.sum.

The main MIT licence is LICENSE. Bundled Go module licence texts are in
LICENSES/dependencies.txt (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause and MPL-2.0).
The MPL component layeh.com/gopher-luar 1.0.11 has source at:
https://github.com/layeh/gopher-luar/tree/v1.0.11

start.sh, launch.py and solve.sh are separate launcher and packaging files.
They apply Landlock and seccomp restrictions and disable user Lua locations;
the editor source and binary are unchanged. This distribution is not
affiliated with or endorsed by the micro project.

Installed executables have mode 0555. The launcher creates execute-only copies
inside the private TMPDIR before applying Landlock; the running program can
execute those copies but cannot read them or the installed implementation as
data. These temporary copies contain unchanged upstream executable bytes.
